From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mariotaku <git@mariotaku.me>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:30:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ui/dbus: read GL scanouts back when they cannot be
 exported as dma-bufs

On Linux, a GL scanout reaches D-Bus listeners only as ScanoutDMABUF,
which needs EGL_MESA_image_dma_buf_export. A surfaceless EGL display on a
driver that is not behind a render node (Mesa d3d12 on WSL2) has none,
so dbus,gl=on could not show anything there.

When the display cannot export dma-bufs, read GL scanouts back instead,
as the Windows SHARE_KIND_MAPPED path does: blit the scanout rectangle
upright into a framebuffer, glReadPixels the damaged rectangle into a
shareable (memfd) a8r8g8b8 surface, and send it with
ScanoutMap/UpdateMap if the listener implements
org.qemu.Display1.Listener.Unix.Map, or copied into Scanout/Update
otherwise. The surface keeps the alpha channel. The console stays
GL-blocked until the listener has handled UpdateMap, like UpdateDMABUF,
so the next frame is not read into the mapping while it is being used.
A scanout texture of the same geometry (a page flip) keeps the listener's
mapping and makes the next update read the whole frame.

Displays that can export dma-bufs are unchanged.
---
 ui/dbus-listener.c | 311 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 ui/trace-events    |   1 +
 2 files changed, 271 insertions(+), 41 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/dbus-listener.c b/ui/dbus-listener.c
